  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you are required to test disaster recovery strategies periodically for a mission-critical application. Which of the following options is the best method to conduct a disaster recovery test while minimizing the impact on production workloads and ensuring high fidelity test results?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Perform a full-scale test by shutting down the production database and simulating a disaster recovery scenario.<br/>B. Introduce random failures to the production environment to test the resilience and recovery strategies in place.<br/>C. Deploy a separate environment identical to the production environment and perform a disaster recovery test using real-time database replication.<br/>D. Use scheduled maintenance windows to simulate disaster recovery scenarios on the production environment.",
